  "method": "All normal-support/interface straight extrusion segments sampled <=0.1mm. Actual line width and layer height; enclosing sphere uses width/2+0.06mm and height/2. Covers nominal segment sampling laterally, not sag, fusing or printed deformation. All04/06 other facets conservatively protected. Interface upper/lower nominal Z-gap projections onto horizontal facets separately classified. Not proof of full deposited filament or removal. Extruder XY offset from actual sliced settings added before inverse object transform. Arcs sampled by I/J center; actual independent support layer heights used. Potential interface projection facets within0.6mm vertically and expanded bead width laterally, independent of support Z-gap rounding. Sphere is only broad-phase. Each candidate protected triangle is clipped to nozzleZ-height-0.005..nozzleZ+0.005; XY distance to the clipped polygon is checked against width/2+0.06. This cylindrical envelope avoids sphere-only false corner contacts. A min-margin of1e10 means no nearby protected facet in the broad-phase, not a measured clearance. Support transition paths also included; XY prefilter uses all arc sample points, not endpoint-only arc bounds. Bead-centre containment candidates from nearest outward face are checked by ray parity; nearest-face sign alone is not used at concave/far corners.",
